From: Justus134 <90705561+Justus134@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:40:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Declare HistoryEventAttributes.sub_type; let scenario steps
 carry app metadata

- HistoryEventAttributes.sub_type is now declared (always None, since history
  resources withhold it), so `ev.attributes.sub_type` reads as None instead of
  raising AttributeError in loops over client.events().
- Scenario steps accept a `meta:` mapping and `x-`-prefixed keys, collected into
  Step.meta and never sent to the emulator. Apps can annotate their own scenario
  files and still replay them with `ring-sandbox play`.
- Unknown step keys now raise a ValueError naming the key and step index, with a
  hint, instead of a raw dataclass TypeError.

Tests cover both changes; ruff check and format pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
